[h2]0.8.5[/h2]
[h3]Reactor Bot workplaces[/h3]
[list]
[*]Every workplace's worker toggle has a third button, [b]Reactor Bots[/b], furthest right. Reactor Bots only work at Reactor Bot workplaces, and bot workplaces take ordinary bots.
[*]Each workplace unlocks it with science: 3 times its bot unlock. Any building can be set to Reactor Bots, including beaver-only and specialist buildings.
[*]The District Center's default worker type has the third option too.
[*]Reactor Bots work at [b]500%[/b] base speed. Left overheating or unplated for too long, they [b]leak radioactive water[/b].
[/list]

[h3]Reactor meltdowns[/h3]
[list]
[*]A meltdown blasts a [b]crater[/b], destroys everything built within [b]6 tiles[/b], and floods the crater with radioactive water that spills over the rim.
[*]Radiation zones are round now, not square.
[/list]

[h3]Modular Warehouse[/h3]
[list]
[*]New [b]Modular Warehouse[/b] and [b]Warehouse Module[/b] (Storage, early game, no power). Attach modules beside it or stack them on top: each adds storage and one more good slot, up to 5, and every slot has its own warehouse settings. Haulers use the one door.
[/list]

[h3]Other changes[/h3]
[list]
[*]Buildings under construction show a construction site and scaffold frame, like vanilla, instead of the finished building.
[*]Farmers and foresters skip irradiated ground instead of replanting it over and over.
[*]Related tools sit together in the menus (Tubeway Stop beside Tubeways; Explosives Factory, Dynamite and Tunnel).
[*]The Fisher Flag says how deep the water must be.
[/list]
